# Frontend Environment

Runtime config is injected at build/deploy time — not hardcoded in TypeScript.

## Mechanism

Each app ships `environments/{dev,stage,production}/env.js` defining `window.__env`:

```js
window.__env.apiUrl = 'http://localhost:8200/v1';
window.__env.environment = 'development';
```

`index.html` loads `env.js` before the app bundle. `EnvironmentService` reads these values at bootstrap.

## Key fields

| Field | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `apiUrl` | Backend base including `/v1` prefix |
| `environment` | `development` / `stage` / `production` |
| `enableDebug` | Console debug toggle |

## Ports (local dev)

| App | Port | Default apiUrl |
|-----|------|----------------|
| Backend | 8200 | — |
| admin-ui | 5100 | `http://localhost:8200/v1` |
| user-ui | 5200 | `http://localhost:8200/v1` |

## Rules

- HTTP services use `this.env.apiUrl` from `BaseApiService` — never literal `localhost` in service code.
- Update all three `env.js` files when adding a new `window.__env` key.
- CORS: backend `app.corsOrigins` must include deployed frontend URLs (see `backend/config/`).

## Reference

- Service: `frontend/projects/common-ui/services/environment.service.ts`
- Factory: `frontend/projects/admin-ui/src/app/core/environment/environment-factory.service.ts`
